WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.561 --> 00:00:20.409
It was early on the morning of January nineteenth when Bessie found me up and nearly dressed.

2
00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:31.151
I was going to school that day on a coach that passed Gateshead at six o'clock. Bessie tried to get me to eat some breakfast, but I was too excited.

3
00:00:31.152 --> 00:00:36.881
As we left the nursery, Bessie said, "Will you say good-bye to Mrs. Reed?"

4
00:00:36.882 --> 00:00:47.041
"No. She came to my bed last night and told me not to disturb her this morning. She also said to remember that she'd always been my best friend."

5
00:00:47.042 --> 00:00:49.218
"And what did you say?"

6
00:00:49.219 --> 00:00:53.390
"Nothing. I turned my face to the wall."

7
00:00:53.391 --> 00:00:59.872
Bessie scolded me but I didn't care. I was leaving Gateshead forever!

8
00:00:59.873 --> 00:01:06.761
Carrying a lantern, she walked me down to the porter's lodge, where my trunk had been sent the night before.

9
00:01:06.761 --> 00:01:13.283
When the coach arrived, my trunk was hoisted up, and I was placed on a seat.

10
00:01:13.284 --> 00:01:24.755
I remembered little of the fifty-mile journey. The afternoon was wet and misty; as darkness fell, we left the towns behind and moved out into open country.

11
00:01:24.756 --> 00:01:29.028
I was lulled to sleep by the wind rushing through the trees.

12
00:01:29.029 --> 00:01:32.583
I woke up when we arrived at Lowood school.

13
00:01:32.584 --> 00:01:39.915
A servant led me through a door in a high wall, and then into a large building with many windows.

14
00:01:39.916 --> 00:01:44.217
We entered a room with a fire, where she left me alone.

15
00:01:44.218 --> 00:01:48.067
A few minutes later, two women entered.

16
00:01:48.068 --> 00:01:54.740
"This child is very young to have been sent alone," said the first woman, whose name was Miss Temple.

17
00:01:54.741 --> 00:02:03.137
She was tall with dark hair and eyes. "Are you tired?" she asked, placing her hand on my shoulder.

18
00:02:03.138 --> 00:02:05.925
"A little, ma'am," I admitted.

19
00:02:05.925 --> 00:02:12.971
"And hungry, too, no doubt. Let her have some supper before she goes to bed, Miss Miller."

20
00:02:12.972 --> 00:02:18.376
Then Miss Temple asked me about my family and whether I could read or write.

21
00:02:18.377 --> 00:02:26.478
She touched my cheek gently. "I hope you'll be a good girl. Now run along with Miss Miller."

22
00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:36.521
Miss Miller, one of the teachers, led me through a maze of corridors until we came to a huge room filled with girls in brown dresses and pinafores.

23
00:02:36.522 --> 00:02:46.259
Seated at long tables and bent over their studies, they appeared countless, though I later learned there were eighty students at the school.

24
00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:52.184
A supper of oat cake and water was soon served, but I was too tired to eat.

25
00:02:52.185 --> 00:03:00.769
The next morning we all sat down to breakfast in the dining hall. A noxious smell came from the basins on the tables.

26
00:03:00.770 --> 00:03:07.689
"Disgusting!" said one of the older girls. "The porridge is burned again."

27
00:03:07.690 --> 00:03:14.338
I tried a mouthful, but burned porridge is almost as bad as rotten potatoes.

28
00:03:14.339 --> 00:03:18.322
Breakfast was over and no one had eaten.

29
00:03:18.323 --> 00:03:24.104
We filed into the schoolroom and at nine o'clock sat down to our lessons.

30
00:03:24.105 --> 00:03:33.017
There were four classes, and I was placed in the lowest. Suddenly everyone rose as Miss Temple entered the room.

31
00:03:33.017 --> 00:03:39.810
Taking her seat near a globe, Miss Temple began giving a geography lesson to the older girls.

32
00:03:39.811 --> 00:03:50.647
The other teachers led classes in history and grammar followed by writing and arithmetic. At last the clock struck twelve, and Miss Temple stood up.

33
00:03:50.648 --> 00:03:59.887
"This morning you had a breakfast that you couldn't eat," she said. "I've ordered a snack of bread and cheese to be served to all."

34
00:03:59.888 --> 00:04:08.214
The girls cheered while the teachers looked at her in surprise. "I'll take responsibility for this," she said.

35
00:04:08.215 --> 00:04:13.720
The bread and cheese were brought in, to the delight of the whole school.

36
00:04:13.721 --> 00:04:17.673
Then the order "To the garden" was given.

37
00:04:17.674 --> 00:04:22.284
Each student put on a coarse straw bonnet and a gray cloak.

38
00:04:22.284 --> 00:04:32.183
I followed the girls outdoors. The garden was a wide space, surrounded by walls so high that they shut out any view.

39
00:04:32.184 --> 00:04:40.502
A covered veranda ran down one side. It was a cold, drizzly day for outdoor exercise.

40
00:04:40.503 --> 00:04:48.757
I had not spoken to anyone yet, nor had anyone noticed me. But I was used to being lonely.

41
00:04:48.758 --> 00:04:55.413
I leaned against a pillar of the verandah and tried to forget both the cold and my hunger.

42
00:04:55.414 --> 00:05:02.343
Presently I noticed a stone tablet over the door that said "Lowood Institution."

43
00:05:02.344 --> 00:05:16.318
I was still pondering the meaning of the word "institution" when the sound of a hollow cough caught my attention. I saw a girl of about 14, sitting on a stone bench.

44
00:05:16.319 --> 00:05:21.624
She was bent over a book; turning a page, she happened to look up.

45
00:05:21.625 --> 00:05:24.899
"Is your book interesting?" I asked.

46
00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:29.916
She paused for a second and examined me. "I like it."

47
00:05:29.917 --> 00:05:31.620
"What's it about?"

48
00:05:31.621 --> 00:05:36.150
"You may look at it." She offered me the book.

49
00:05:36.151 --> 00:05:43.300
I'd hoped that the book would contain fairy tales, but there was nothing like that on its densely printed pages.

50
00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:48.677
I returned it, and she was about to start reading again when I interrupted her.

51
00:05:48.678 --> 00:05:52.635
"Why is this place called an institution?"

52
00:05:52.636 --> 00:06:03.788
"We're all charity children," the girl explained. "Everyone has lost one or both parents, and this is an institution for educating orphans.

53
00:06:03.789 --> 00:06:10.288
We, or our friends, pay fifteen pounds a year so that we can stay here."

54
00:06:10.289 --> 00:06:15.931
I was still puzzled. "Then why do they call us charity children?"

55
00:06:15.931 --> 00:06:25.207
"Because fifteen pounds isn't enough to cover the cost of our living here. The rest is made up by subscriptions from benevolent people."

56
00:06:25.208 --> 00:06:38.523
I asked more questions, and the girl explained that Mr. Brocklehurst was the treasurer and manager of Lowood. A clergyman, he lived in a fine, large house two miles away.

57
00:06:38.524 --> 00:06:43.076
"So the school doesn't belong to Miss Temple?" I asked.

58
00:06:43.077 --> 00:06:53.660
"I wish it did! She has to answer to Mr. Brocklehurst for everything she does as superintendent. He buys all our clothes and food."

59
00:06:53.661 --> 00:06:55.747
"Are you happy here?"

60
00:06:55.747 --> 00:07:00.821
"You ask too many questions. I want to read."

61
00:07:00.822 --> 00:07:06.069
But I asked one more and learned that her name was Helen Burns.

62
00:07:06.070 --> 00:07:10.590
Just then the bell sounded for lunch, so we filed inside.

63
00:07:10.591 --> 00:07:20.713
The odor that filled the dining hall was scarcely more appetizing than at breakfast. I could eat little of the fatty meat and gray potatoes.

64
00:07:20.714 --> 00:07:26.481
After lunch we adjourned to the schoolroom, where lessons continued until five o'clock.

65
00:07:26.482 --> 00:07:37.459
During the afternoon Miss Scatcherd, one of the teachers, dismissed Helen in disgrace from history class and forced her to stand in the middle of the schoolroom.

66
00:07:37.460 --> 00:07:50.777
It seemed a terrible punishment to me, but Helen neither wept nor blushed. And I was left to wonder whether she was a good or naughty child.
